From: Derek Ross <derekross@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 13:42:14 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 14/14] pipeline: simple: Accept a sensor configuration within
 1% of the stream

The simple pipeline handler picks the smallest sensor configuration
whose largest processed output covers every processed stream. The
software ISP's debayer leaves a margin of 8 columns, so a binned sensor
mode exactly as wide as a common stream size never covers it: the Pixel
7 Pro's front camera has a 1920x1368 binned mode (1912 columns out) and
a 3840x2736 full one, and a 1920x1080 video stream runs the full mode,
four times the data to read and debayer per frame.

Let a configuration whose largest output falls short by at most 1% in
each direction qualify as well. The existing stream adjustment then
brings the stream down to what the configuration delivers (1912x1080
there) and reports the configuration as adjusted. A request now gets
the smaller sensor mode whenever one is within 1% of it, at the cost of
up to 1% of the stream's size.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/libcamera/pipeline/simple/simple.cpp | 15 +++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/libcamera/pipeline/simple/simple.cpp b/src/libcamera/pipeline/simple/simple.cpp
index 9fa4cce..6a5b399 100644
--- a/src/libcamera/pipeline/simple/simple.cpp
+++ b/src/libcamera/pipeline/simple/simple.cpp
@@ -1234,12 +1234,23 @@ CameraConfiguration::Status SimpleCameraConfiguration::validate()
 	const SimpleCameraData::Configuration *maxPipeConfig = nullptr;
 	pipeConfig_ = nullptr;
 
+	/*
+	 * A configuration whose largest output is short of the processed
+	 * streams by at most 1% in each direction qualifies too, and the
+	 * streams are adjusted down to it below. The converter may need a
+	 * margin (the software ISP's debayer leaves 8 columns), so a binned
+	 * sensor mode exactly as wide as the request would otherwise lose to a
+	 * full-resolution one, at four times the data per frame.
+	 */
+	const Size nearProcessedStreamSize{ maxProcessedStreamSize.width * 99 / 100,
+					    maxProcessedStreamSize.height * 99 / 100 };
+
 	for (const SimpleCameraData::Configuration *pipeConfig : *configs) {
 		const Size &captureSize = pipeConfig->captureSize;
 		const Size &maxOutputSize = pipeConfig->outputSizes.max;
 
-		if (maxOutputSize.width >= maxProcessedStreamSize.width &&
-		    maxOutputSize.height >= maxProcessedStreamSize.height &&
+		if (maxOutputSize.width >= nearProcessedStreamSize.width &&
+		    maxOutputSize.height >= nearProcessedStreamSize.height &&
 		    captureSize.width >= maxRawStreamSize.width &&
 		    captureSize.height >= maxRawStreamSize.height) {
 			if (!pipeConfig_ || captureSize < pipeConfig_->captureSize)
